{{Quote|You cannot surprise a Gand. We see the moves before they happen.|Zuckuss, to 4-LOM|<ref name="Bounty Hunters 20">[[Bounty Hunters 20|''Bounty Hunters'' 20]]</ref>}}
'''Gand''' were an [[insectoid]] [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]] [[Homeworld|native]] to the [[planet]] [[Gand (planet)|Gand]]. [[Breathing Gand|One]] [[subspecies]] breathed [[ammonia]], forcing them to wear [[Breath mask|respirators]] to survive in [[oxygen]]-rich [[atmosphere]]s. A notable member of this species was [[Zuckuss]], a [[bounty hunter]] who was one of the first traditional [[Findsman|findsmen]] to leave his homeworld.

==Biology and appearance==
{{Quote|And what's with the stink? The place smells like a bantha pen.''"<br />"''The gasses remind Zuckuss of his homeworld.|Han Solo and 4-LOM|<ref name="Hunter vs Hunted">[[Star Wars Adventures Free Comic Book Day 2018|''Star Wars Adventures'' Free Comic Book Day 2018]]</ref>}}
[[File:MasklessZuckuss-BountyHunters15.png|thumb|left|250px|The Gand Zuckuss without his respirator]]
Gand were a stocky, three-[[Limb|fingered]],<ref name="The Empire Strikes Back" /> two-toed,<ref name="Zuckuss Sideshow">{{SideshowCite|set=Sideshow Collectibles|text=Sixth Scale Figures|pack=Zuckuss|altlink=https://www.sideshowtoy.com/collectibles/star-wars-zuckuss-sideshow-collectibles-100316}}</ref> [[insectoid]] [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]]<ref name="Updated and Expanded" /> with [[Color|brown]] skin whose heads featured a pair of large, silver<ref name="The Empire Strikes Back" /> compound [[eye]]s.<ref name="Updated and Expanded" />

There existed two [[subspecies]] of Gand: [[Breathing Gand|one]] that breathed [[ammonia]], a compound that made up most of the [[atmosphere]] of their [[homeworld]] of [[Gand (planet)|Gand]], and [[Non-breathing Gand|another]] that did not breathe at all, drawing its sustenance by absorption from its food intake and approximating speech by modulating the sounds of its flatulence.<ref name="BMF 43" />

Ammonia-breathing Gand had to wear [[Breath mask|respirators]] over their [[mouth]]s in order to breath in [[oxygen]]-rich environments.<ref name="Updated and Expanded" /> In terms of genetics, Gand were distantly related to the [[Kel Dor]] and [[Tognath]] species, who similarly wore masks when off their homeworlds.<ref name="R1 UVG">''[[Star Wars: Rogue One: The Ultimate Visual Guide]]''</ref>

==Society and culture==
{{Quote|The Gand should not leave Gand. It is not the way.|Churkk|<ref name="Phasma">[[Phasma (novel)|''Phasma'']]</ref>}}
Some Gand were [[Findsman|findsmen]], a mystic tradition that dated back [[Standard century|centuries]] on their fog-shrouded homeworld who were known for their uncanny tracking skills.<ref name="Updated and Expanded" /> The species spoke a [[language]] of the [[Gand (language)|same name]].<ref name="Endless Vigil" /> It was against Gand tradition for them to leave their homeworld. If they spoke their last name, it often meant they were remotely ashamed.<ref name="Phasma" />

==Gand in the galaxy==
{{Quote|Something isn't right. Zuckuss can sense it.''"<br />"''How many times must I remind you, Zuckuss? I deal with facts, not superstitious flim-flam.|Zuckuss and 4-LOM|<ref name="Powered Down I">{{IDWAdventuresCite-2017|issue=10|story=Powered Down, Part 1}}</ref>}}
[[File:Gand_FDEV.png|thumb|right|180px|A Gand Jedi Sentinel]]
Gand [[Spy|spies]] and [[engineer]]s were some of the most renowned in [[the galaxy]]. Many Gand found themselves forced into the Empire's services.<ref name="RCC">{{Disney|subdomain=lol|url=games/star-wars-rebels-chopper-chase|text=Star Wars Rebels: Chopper Chase|int=Star Wars Rebels: Chopper Chase|nolive=1}}</ref> Originally from the [[planet]] of the same name<ref name="Updated and Expanded" /> located in the galaxy's [[Outer Rim Territories]],<ref name="Beginner Game">[[Star Wars: The Force Awakens Beginner Game|''Star Wars: The Force Awakens'' Beginner Game]]</ref> [[Rinn (Gand)|Rinn]] was a Gand [[bounty hunter]] who took a [[Mission to Ord Mantell (Jango Fett)|job]] with [[Jango Fett]] sometime before the [[plot to assassinate Senator Amidala]].<ref name="Age of Republic">[[Age of Republic - Jango Fett 1|''Age of Republic - Jango Fett'' 1]]</ref> Sometime between [[5 BBY]] and [[4 BBY]],<ref name="RCC Date Note">{{ChopperChaseDate}}</ref>
a Gand engineer was forced by the Empire to build the ship model, the ''[[Blackburn]]'', but the engineer was later rescued by the [[Spectres]].<ref name="RCC" /> A Gand inhabited [[Nar Shaddaa]], which was nicknamed the "[[Smuggler]]'s [[Moon]]," during the [[Galactic Civil War]],<ref name="Showdown on the Smuggler's Moon, Part III">[[Star Wars (2015) 10|''Star Wars'' (2015) 10]]</ref> and another served aboard the [[starship]] ''[[Espirion Multi]]''.<ref name="Princess Leia, Part V">[[Princess Leia 5|''Princess Leia'' 5]]</ref> A [[Gender|male]] Gand [[bounty]] hunter known as [[Zuckuss]] was one of the first findsmen to leave their homeworld when the tradition was dying out.<ref name="Updated and Expanded" /> [[Churkk]] was a Gand who left Gand at a young age before becoming stranded on [[Parnassos]], where he lived the rest of his life.<ref name="Phasma" />

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:ZuckussConceptArt.jpg|thumb|left|250px|Concept art of Zuckuss by John Mollo]]
The Gand species first appeared in the [[1980]] film [[Star Wars: Episode V The Empire Strikes Back|''Star Wars'': Episode V ''The Empire Strikes Back'']] as the then-unnamed species of the bounty hunter Zuckuss.<ref name="The Empire Strikes Back" /> Portrayed by actress [[Cathy Munro|Catherine Monroe]], the character's features were designed by [[Ralph McQuarrie]] and [[John Mollo]], and the mask was crafted by [[Stuart Freeborn]]. The compound eyes of the mask were constructed with [[Wikipedia:Bubble wrap|bubble wrap]] packing material, while the costume itself consisted of the full-head mask and attached cylinders that were filled with colored water, and the actress was instructed to blow air into the cylinders in order to create bubbles.<ref name="MunroeInterview">{{WebCite|url=http://www.starwarsaficionado.com/f/CATHERINE_MUNROE_INTERVIEW1.pdf|text=Catherine Munroe Interview - Conversations with a Bounty Hunter!!|archivedate=20130927184813}}</ref>

Zuckuss's species was first identified as Gand in ''[[Galaxy Guide 3: The Empire Strikes Back]]'', a [[1989]] [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] supplement written by [[Michael Stern]] for ''[[Star Wars: The Roleplaying Game]]''.<ref name="The Empire Strikes Back" /> This name became [[canon]] when it was utilized in Zuckuss's entry in ''[[Ultimate Star Wars]]'', a reference book co-written by [[Tricia Barr|Patricia Barr]], [[Adam Bray]], [[Daniel Wallace]], and [[Ryder Windham]]<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars">''[[Ultimate Star Wars]]''</ref> that was released on [[April 28]], [[2015]].<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars release date">{{DK|url=us/book/9781465436016-ultimate-star-wars|text=Ultimate Star Wars|nolive=1}}</ref>

